[{:seon.task/name "source-at-the-repl"
  :seon.task/plan "Agents read code the way a Clojure REPL does, and on Jolt that fails. Mined from T5 real run 3 (t5/out/real3.store, 2026-10-20): 4 of 8 agents evaluated (clojure.repl/source f), (clojure.repl/source-fn 'ns/f) or (require '[clojure.repl :refer [source]]) 171 times (\"No such var: clojure.repl/source\", \"source does not exist\"), and 3 agents tried (slurp (clojure.java.io/resource \"t5/forgive_test.clj\")) 53 times (\"Cannot open <nil> as a Reader\"): program code lives as facts (:var/src, :ns/src), not files. R4's run hit the same (20 times). What would a plain Clojure REPL do? `source` prints the definition and `source-fn` answers its text. In an agent, clojure.repl/source-fn and source answer a var's exact recorded text from the branch's db (seon.context/source-of), and doc works as at any REPL. Estimate: one AVET seek per call (seon.task/eid's cost)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.repl-test/source-answers-a-program-definition-from-its-facts}}
 {:seon.task/name "eval-record-keeps-a-failing-form-whole"
  :seon.task/plan "An eval record's :form is the form printed under the :form budget (600 tokens), so a failing form is cut (…N): mining T5 real run 3 could not read the whole defn that failed in t5.refusal/describe (it had to be recovered from the model's reply). Record the exact text the agent sent for a form that errs (N1 already cuts exact text from the reader's positions for defs: :var/src), bounded only by the request itself; a form that succeeds keeps its printed echo. Cost follows the failing forms only."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.repl-test/a-failing-form-is-recorded-whole}}
 {:seon.task/name "source-reads-the-program"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by the first DeepSeek agent on Seon's own code (2026-10-21, `seon.fences/a-refused-spawn-is-recorded`, 8 turns spent exploring, no fix written): `(clojure.repl/source seon.reconcile/stuck)` and the same for `advance`, `write`, `cas-tx`, `index` error in an agent's REPL (IllegalArgumentException or ExceptionInfo), because a compiled platform var has no source file the agent process can read. The program facts hold every form's exact text (`:form/src`, imported by `seon.source`; `seon.context/source-of` already reads it). An agent's REPL is a real Clojure REPL (AGENTS.md: get out of an agent's way), so `source` and `clojure.repl/source-fn` answer a var's recorded form text from the agent's branch db (its own redefinition if it made one), the way `doc` does, for platform and program vars alike. One reader: reuse `seon.context/source-of`, no second lookup."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.repl-test/source-answers-a-platform-var-from-the-program}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-reloaded-file-is-the-branchs-change"
  :seon.task/plan "Measured 2026-10-21 on the standing root: the agent on `seon.root/a-proc-answers-every-request-it-took` worked the way Clojure users do: it edited `src/seon/root.clj` with a string replace (`spit`), then `(require 'seon.root :reload)` and `(clojure.test/run-tests 'seon.procs-test)`; 17 turns, 5.5M tokens, and its branch recorded none of it, because only forms evaluated through the one REPL path (`seon.repl/eval-code`) are recorded as the branch's program (`seon.program/record-tx`), so its proofs ran on the unchanged program (`:no-assertions`) and the merge would carry nothing. The owner: match a real Clojure REPL and improve on it. Correct: in an agent, `require` with `:reload` (or `:reload-all`) of a namespace whose file is in the agent's directory, and `load-file` of such a file, evaluate that file's forms through the one REPL path in that namespace, so each form is recorded on the branch exactly as if it had been evaluated at the REPL (as nREPL's load-file op already does in `seon.repl/base-handler`: \"load-file\" -> `eval-code`); a form that did not change records nothing new (`seon.program/record-tx` supersedes by content). Nothing else changes: a file written and never loaded is the agent's scratch. Extends the REPL path; no watcher, no second loader."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.repl-test/an-edited-file-reloaded-is-the-branchs-program}}
 {:seon.task/name "an-eval-error-never-ends-the-attempt"
  :seon.task/plan "Measured 2026-10-22 06:4x on the standing root: attempt `seon.root/a-proc-answers-every-request-it-took#1` ended `:closed :error`, turns 0, reason \"seon.turn/work! threw: No matching field found: exists for class java.lang.String\", error `{:seon.error/type :seon.agent/eval-error :seon.error/operation seon.repl/eval-code :class IllegalArgumentException}`; its branch shows it re-evaluated every form of `my.root` (the ns form and each defn, unchanged text), most likely by `(require 'my.root :reload)` or `load-file` through `seon.repl/loaded-form` (lane RELOAD, jolt.host/*load-form*). An evaluation error is the agent's to read (a reply item with :tag :err), never the end of its attempt; this one escaped `seon.repl/eval-code` into `seon.turn/work!`, and the turn was not recorded, so the form that raised it is lost. A plain `(load-file \"src/my/root.clj\")` and `(require 'my.root :reload)` in a fresh agent answer nil (not reproduced). Correct: find the form and path that raise it (reload my.root after the agent's other turn-0 forms; a load whose form calls a File method on a path string), make every error raised while a loaded file's forms evaluate reach the agent as that load's :err item (Clojure's: the require throws, the REPL prints it), and record the turn before anything after the evaluation can fail. Proof: the reproducing forms in an agent answer an :err item and the agent takes its next turn."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.repl-test/an-error-inside-a-loaded-file-is-the-loads-error-item}}]
